#!/bin/bash
# land-gem-sheets.sh — the gemstone pages become the owner's reference, and
# every stone says how many carats this person is prescribed.
#
# BOTH SIDES (together-city-chat + together-city-react). Vercel AND Railway.
# PRECONDITION: land-gemstones-tab.sh.
set -euo pipefail

cd "$(dirname "$0")"
[ -d together-city-chat ] || { echo "!! Run this from the Together-Ai repo root."; exit 1; }

if [ -f .git/index.lock ] && [ ! -s .git/index.lock ]; then
  echo "== clearing a stale empty .git/index.lock"
  rm -f .git/index.lock
fi

NEEDS="A price per carat is not a price"
LOG="$(git log --oneline -40)"
case "$LOG" in
  *"$NEEDS"*) echo "== \"$NEEDS\" is already here. Nothing to do."; exit 0 ;;
esac
case "$LOG" in
  *"One surface prescribes a stone"*) ;;
  *) echo "!! Run land-gemstones-tab.sh first — this is written against the tree it produces."; exit 1 ;;
esac

ALLOWED='^ M together-city-react/(public/assets/img/(apple-touch-icon-180|tc-icon-1024|tc-icon-192|tc-icon-512|tc-icon-maskable-512)\.png|public/downloads/TogetherCity\.apk)$'
DIRTY="$(git status --porcelain \
  | grep -Ev '^\?\? (land-.*\.sh|push-.*\.sh|.*\.patch)$' \
  | grep -Ev "$ALLOWED" || true)"
if [ -n "$DIRTY" ]; then
  echo "!! The tree carries changes this script did not expect:"; echo "$DIRTY"; exit 1
fi

PATCH="$(mktemp "${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/land.XXXXXX")"
trap 'rm -f "$PATCH"' EXIT
cat <<'B64EOF' | tr -d '\n' | openssl base64 -d -A > "$PATCH"

B64EOF
WANT="3d46351fc2cf8eaaef2e8c50d3bd9f8577af635818eeefc5bf080400599e8a3d"
GOT="$(shasum -a 256 "$PATCH" | awk '{print $1}')"
[ "$GOT" = "$WANT" ] || { echo "!! Patch is corrupt."; echo "   want $WANT"; echo "   got  $GOT"; exit 1; }
echo "== patch verified"
git apply --check -C1 "$PATCH" || { echo "!! Patch does not apply cleanly. Nothing written."; exit 1; }
git apply -C1 "$PATCH"
echo "== applied"

echo "== gates: the API"
cd together-city-chat
npx tsc --noEmit
npx jest src/astrology
cd ..

echo "== gates: the web app"
cd together-city-react
npx tsc --noEmit
npx vitest run
node scripts/a11y-audit.mjs
node scripts/motion-ceiling.mjs
node scripts/lint-ceiling.mjs
npx vite build
cd ..

git add together-city-chat/src/astrology/gems \
        together-city-chat/src/astrology/astrology.service.ts \
        together-city-react/src/features/astrology \
        together-city-react/src/styles/layout.css \
        together-city-react/src/app/relief.spec.ts \
        together-city-react/src/app/one-energy.test.ts \
        together-city-react/src/app/one-stone-answer.test.ts
git commit -F - <<'MSG'
A price per carat is not a price

Two things, and the second is the one that makes the page useful.

THE SHEETS ARE THE OWNER'S REFERENCE NOW. The first build was a photograph on
the left and a grey grid of facts on the right — a perfectly good product row
that threw the entire composition away. The reference makes each stone A PAGE: a
capsule at the top, three trait words arched over the photograph, the name
beneath in engraved capitals, warm prose under that, a price ring at the foot,
centred the whole way down. Two stones side by side stop being pages and start
being products, so they never are.

Everything this page adds beyond the reference is said in the reference's own
vocabulary — a tracked label and a centred paragraph, nothing new invented. WHY
THIS STONE, FOR YOU goes first because it is the only section written about the
reader. HOW IT IS WORN carries the finger, the hand, the metal and the day. WORN
ON TRIAL FIRST appears on the three stones that need it. The one deliberate
deviation is the badge: the reference numbers each card, and here the stones are
ordered by what they do for THIS chart, so a "3" on the first sheet would answer
a question nobody asked. It carries the role instead.

AND EVERY SHEET SAYS HOW MANY CARATS. "8,000 - 25,000 per carat" is not a price.
It tells somebody nothing until they know how many carats they are prescribed,
and that is a property of the WEARER, not of the stone. The tradition's own rule
is one ratti for every ten kilos of body weight, at the data sheet's 0.91 ct to
the ratti — so 70 kg is 7 ratti is 6.37 ct, shown as 6.25 because stones are cut
in quarter carats. The body weight comes from the Master Profile, already
entered once. The sheet names the rule, gives the workable spread either side,
and says to have a jeweller or astrologer confirm it.

NO BODY WEIGHT MEANS NO FIGURE. Not an average, not "most people wear five" —
the same refusal the ascendant gets without a birth time, and for a larger sum
of money. The substitutes are priced at the heavier weight the tradition asks of
them, which is the number that decides whether a stone at a fifth of the
per-carat price is actually cheaper.

Three things worth writing down:

  · THE COLOUR IS THE CATALOGUE'S, NOT THE PAGE'S. Each sheet is themed to its
    stone. relief.spec forbids colour written into a page and is right to; these
    arrive in the payload beside the photograph and are applied as custom
    properties, and a test now fails if a hex is ever typed into this file.

  · THE SERIF IS A FIFTH GRANT, ASKED FOR PROPERLY. `.gem-display` joins the
    letter title, the archive day and the routine masthead in relief.spec's
    by-name list, with its own reason: at .34em of tracking that name is closer
    to engraving than to a heading, and the sans cannot do it.

  · A GUARD FIRED ON A COINCIDENCE. one-energy.test.ts hunts a fifth
    Mifflin-St Jeor implementation by its coefficients, and a bare 6.25 was one
    of them — which is not a fingerprint, it is a number. It caught a gemstone
    weighing 6.25 carats in a file with no metabolism arithmetic in it. The
    height term is matched against a height now. A guard that fires on a
    coincidence teaches people to add themselves to its allow list, and an allow
    list is where a guard goes to die.

The arc took three goes and each failure is in the CSS. Left at 100% width the
words float an inch above the stone; capped at the viewBox width they fit but an
inline <svg> tucks up beside the role capsule; and text longer than its path is
clipped rather than wrapped, so "VITALITY - COURAGE - PASSION" rendered as
"ITALITY - COURAGE - PASSIO". It is a block, the pull is -25% so it survives a
resize, and the type is sized for the longest trait line in the catalogue rather
than for the ruby's.
MSG

echo "== committed"
cat <<'DONE'

===============================================================
 Landed: A price per carat is not a price
 Both sides — push, then give Railway a minute before opening
 Astrology -> Gemstones.
===============================================================

DONE
